# {Project Name} — Standards

Read these before writing code. They are the project's standards, not suggestions.

- `standards/core/guardrails.md` — **overrides everything else.** Commit approval,
  no attribution trailers, no credential access, honest reporting
- `standards/core/rules.md` — limits, types, naming, errors, comments, docs
- `standards/platform/{web|native}.md` — whichever this project installed
- `standards/framework/{stack}.md` — whichever this project installed

`standards/core/rules.md` opens with a routing table mapping each kind of task to
the `standards/reference/…` file to read first. Follow it. Those files are
deliberately not loaded up front.

## Workflows

`workflows/*.md` are prompt documents for recurring tasks — component scaffolding,
tests, review, PR prep, audits, visual verification. When asked to do one, read
the file and follow it. `workflows/` lists the full set.

## Project specifics

Deviations go here, never in `standards/` — that directory is shared and gets
overwritten on sync.

- **Stack:** {nextjs | react | vue | angular | react-native}
- **Project mode:** {greenfield | legacy}
- **Project policy:** `standards/project.json` (thresholds, strictness, stack choices, commands)
- **Component library:** {package, docs URL}
- **i18n:** {library and locales path, or "single locale"}
- **Test utils:** `@/utils/test-utils`
- **Deviations:** {none, or list with reason + owner + review date}

